# Agent policy source of truth

**Do not** look for `AGENTS.md`, debate it, or ask about it. It is gitignored
and usually absent on Cloud VMs — it cannot enforce anything here.

## What actually sticks across Cloud sessions

| Mechanism | Sticks on Cloud? |
|---|---|
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (`alwaysApply: true`) | **Yes** (in git) |
| [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) | **Yes** (in git) |
| Cursor User Rules / Team Rules | Yes (account/dashboard, not git) |
| Workspace `AGENTS.md` | **No** if gitignored |

Put non‑negotiables in `.cursor/rules/` (short `.mdc` files). That *is*
enforcement. Do not re‑create a giant `AGENTS.md` in git.

## In this repo

- `git-workflow.mdc` — branch / PR naming
- `releases.mdc` — **Current trains** mapping; cherry-pick / merge-back procedures
- `coding-standards.mdc` — no essay comments
- `changelog.mdc` — product only (not website); never edit dated sections.
  That file is the split; do not restate or drift from it here.
- `verification.mdc` — always run ruff / mypy / pytest
